ORIGIN

This skill is original work by Seth J. Chandler. It encodes a workflow for
creating and validating fictional commercial mediation-competition problems,
including a canonical case model, asymmetric confidential packets, a narrow
settlement corridor, deterministic checks, and semantic role-limited audits.

The Lawve distribution package reorganizes the original reference materials
under resources/, adds portable capability fallbacks, catalogue metadata,
jurisdiction and confidentiality disclosures, and this licence and notice. It
does not alter the substantive problem-design methodology.

This skill is not affiliated with or endorsed by Lawve, any mediation
competition, or any dispute-resolution institution.

---

BUNDLED CODE

Three Python 3 scripts are included. Each uses only the Python standard library;
none makes network calls, spawns subprocesses, handles credentials, or evaluates
dynamic code.

- scripts/scaffold_case_model.py creates a starter JSON model at a path named by
  the caller and refuses to overwrite an existing file unless --force is used.
- scripts/validate_case_model.py reads a case-model JSON file and writes findings
  only when the caller supplies --report with an output path.
- scripts/check_information_firewall.py reads the model and packet files and
  reports possible verbatim confidential-fact leakage; it writes no files.

